Kenney Input Prompts
===================

Controller prompts and controller silhouettes use Kenney Input Prompts 1.5A,
distributed under Creative Commons Zero (CC0 1.0 Universal). The selected SVGs
have cropped view boxes and dark-ink variants for light surfaces.

https://kenney.nl/assets/input-prompts
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Qt 6
====

The OpenNOW desktop shell dynamically links Qt 6 Core, GUI, QML, Quick,
Quick Controls, Network and Multimedia modules. Open-source Qt builds are used
under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3. The packaged
LGPL-3.0-only.txt contains the complete license and users may replace the
dynamically linked Qt libraries with compatible modified versions.

https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations

SDL
===

The Qt shell dynamically links SDL 3 for controller input. The native streamer
also embeds the Rust SDL 2 binding and its SDL runtime. SDL is distributed under
the zlib license; the complete SDL3-LICENSE.txt is packaged beside this notice,
and the generated Rust dependency section includes the resolved SDL 2 notices.

https://www.libsdl.org/

FFmpeg
======

Bundled Linux builds statically link FFmpeg through ffmpeg-sys-next. FFmpeg's
default combined license is LGPL-2.1-or-later; the binding crate's WTFPL does
not replace FFmpeg's license. These builds do not enable GPL, version3, or
nonfree components. The complete LGPL 2.1 text and upstream licensing details
are packaged as FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt and FFmpeg-LICENSE.md.

Linux ARM64 bundled builds use the Raspberry Pi FFmpeg fork at the immutable
commit f43bd9dafd9349b6824ee1fdcd967662fcc94c20:
https://github.com/jc-kynesim/rpi-ffmpeg/tree/f43bd9dafd9349b6824ee1fdcd967662fcc94c20

Its SAND and V4L2 request additions also contain BSD-3-Clause and MIT-licensed
code. Their copyright and license notices are packaged in
FFmpeg-Raspberry-Pi-NOTICES.txt. Other Linux architectures retain the upstream
FFmpeg release/9.0 source path: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/release/9.0

The OpenNOW source distribution contains the build configuration in
native/opennow-streamer/vendor/ffmpeg-sys-next/build.rs and the Qt/Rust build
files needed to rebuild the application with modified FFmpeg libraries.
The fetched FFmpeg checkout preserves its original copyright and COPYING
files. Distributors of a statically linked binary must provide its exact
corresponding FFmpeg source and the materials required to relink against a
modified compatible FFmpeg, as required by LGPL 2.1 section 6. A source URL
or this notice alone does not replace those distribution obligations.

OpenH264
========

The software decoder fallback builds Cisco OpenH264 from source through the
openh264 Rust package. OpenH264 is available under the BSD 2-Clause license;
the complete OpenH264-LICENSE.txt is packaged beside this notice.

https://github.com/cisco/openh264

Lucide
======

The Qt desktop shell uses Lucide 1.31.0 icons, recolored to match the OpenNOW
interface. Lucide is available under the ISC license, with icons derived from
Feather also covered by the MIT license. The complete Lucide-LICENSE.txt is
packaged beside this notice.

https://lucide.dev/

